<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct industrial output rises 3.5 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct industrial output rises 3.5 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production rose a preliminary 3.5 percent in October from the previous month on a seasonally adjusted basis, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>MITI said that industrial production was on a gradual uptrend.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of the preliminary monthly figures follows:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>				  OCT     MONTH AGO     OCT INDEX</p>
<p> Output			 +3.5	+1.5	 101.1</p>
<p> Shipments		    +3.3	+1.8	 102.6</p>
<p> Inventories		  +0.6	-1.0	 108.2</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	 -3.7	-0.9	 111.5</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (in pct):</p>
<p>				   OCT     MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output			  +6.0	+3.8</p>
<p> Shipments		     +6.4	+3.6</p>
<p> Inventories		   -0.2	+0.3</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	 -5.5	-1.2</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of MITI's forecasts for manufacturers' output:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted, month-on-month (in pct):</p>
<p>		     NOV forecast   DEC forecast</p>
<p>		     -1.7	     -0.2</p>
